ll in the world. It is situated in Kothmale area, on the A5 highway at Ramboda Pass. The waterfall is formed by the Panna Oya which is a tributary of Kothmale Oya. The falls have an elevation 945\u00a0m (3,100\u00a0ft) above sea level.", "extract_html": "<p><b>Ramboda Falls</b> is 109\u00a0m (358\u00a0ft) high and the eleventh tallest waterfall in Sri Lanka and the 729th tallest waterfall in the world. It is situated in Kothmale area, on the A5 highway at Ramboda Pass. The waterfall is formed by the Panna Oya which is a tributary of Kothmale Oya. The falls have an elevation 945\u00a0m (3,100\u00a0ft) above sea level.</p>"}